WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.790
All the heroes of the Marvel Cinematic Universe
are gearing up for Avengers: Endgame but one

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.960
beloved character seems to be MIA and it’s
not sitting well with fans.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.240
After a massive blast of 32 character posters
for the upcoming crossover event hit the web,

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.460
fans immediately took to social media with
one question: where the heck is Korg?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.340
In case you missed it, a bit of background:
when the God of Thunder was tossed into the

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:27.380
Grandmaster's dungeon on the planet Sakaar
early on in 2017's Thor: Ragnarok Korg was

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.880
the first to make his acquaintance.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.220
“Allow me to introduce myself.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.230
My name is Korg.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.680
I’m kind of like the leader in here.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.000
I’m made of rocks, as you can see, but don’t
let that intimidate you.”

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.680
He's huge, blue, and made of rocks and although
he has a most genial manner, he's something

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.180
of a budding revolutionary.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.820
Later in the film, Korg and his companion
Miek join Thor and his team of "Revengers"

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.520
in their bid to prevent the destruction of
Asgard, which doesn't go super-well.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.030
When Thor's insanely formidable sister Hela,
the goddess of Death, appears ready to wipe

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.711
out Asgard's citizens, the makeshift team
is forced to unleash the demon Surtur, who

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.740
lays waste to the realm — and kills Hela
in the process.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.760
As the beast embarks on its rampage, Korg
helpfully provides commentary:

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.120
"The damage isn't too bad, as long as the foundations are still strong.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.940
"we can rebuild this place."

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:17.880
“Oof!

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.180
Now those foundations are gone.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:19.680
Sorry."

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.880
The Endgame posters trickled out over the
course of a day, and as one-sheets for the

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.490
Asgardian warrior Valkyrie and the fallen
trickster god Loki dropped, true believers

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.880
waited anxiously for Korg to get his due.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.480
But, alas, it never happened.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.320
It should probably be mentioned that Korg
was portrayed by Thor: Ragnarok director Taika

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.920
Waititi, who has been just a little bit busy.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.290
In addition to creating a small screen adaptation
of his 2014 comedy feature What We Do in the

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:50.700
Shadows for FX, Waititi helmed and appeared
in the forthcoming dramedy Jojo Rabbit, and

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:56.180
has been lending his vocal talent to several
episodes of the currently-in-production Disney+

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.560
series The Mandalorian.

00:01:58.049 --> 00:02:02.479
On top of all this, he's serving as a producer
on the feature We're Wolves, as well as Time

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:07.890
Bandits, a TV adaptation of Terry Gilliam's
classic 1981 film which recently received

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.960
a pilot order from Apple's soon-to-debut streaming
service.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.459
With all of this on his plate, Waititi can
perhaps be forgiven for not lobbying too hard

00:02:15.459 --> 00:02:19.760
to return as the big blue revolutionary in
Endgame — but that didn't keep fans far

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.780
and wide from expressing their disappointment.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.740
Compounding the omission is the fact that
the character's fate was left unclear; while

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.109
he was present for the flight of the Asgardians
aboard the Grandmaster's spaceship at Ragnarok's

00:02:30.109 --> 00:02:34.879
conclusion, he was nowhere to be seen during
Avengers: Infinity War's brutal opening sequence

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:40.160
aboard that very ship, in which Thanos murders
Heimdall, snaps Loki's neck, and slaps a fully

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.080
enraged Hulk around like a rag doll.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.560
This oversight didn't sit well with fans,
many of whom politely suggested that a little

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.069
clarification was in order.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:52.329
There is a bright side to all this: at least
Korg didn't get one of those black-and-white

00:02:52.329 --> 00:02:56.980
"dusted" posters, which is more than we can
say for Loki not to mention T'Challa's little

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.200
sister Shuri.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.400
Perhaps Korg actually defeats Thanos in Endgame,
which at least one fan suggested on Twitter.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.099
We can almost get on board with this, although
we're not quite sure that trying to kill the

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.840
Mad Titan with kindness is really the way
to go.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.879
At any rate, hopefully Marvel will remember
Korg as it brings closure to the arcs of a

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.860
ridiculous number of heroes in Avengers: Endgame,.

